 "researcher_notes": "EIA August 2026 release, sheet Historical Projects, Excel row 681: new intrastate pipeline in Texas, completed 17 Feb 2011, 50 mi, 24 in, 400 MMcf/d, owner Energy Transfer Partners LP. A Pipeline and Gas Journal item from February 2011 (page now 404, not cited) and World Pipelines from October 2010 say the same, and an Oil and Gas Journal item from October 2010 names the project. World Pipelines describes it as running from northwest Webb County to the Houston Pipeline rich gas gathering system in eastern Webb County, with Dec 2010 target completion. Checked the US gas roster: no row named Dos Hermanas. Nearest is P0224 (NET Mexico Gas Pipeline, Agua Dulce), a different line. Meets the length rule (50 mi is over 15.5 mi). Owner is the 2011 Energy Transfer Partners LP, now Energy Transfer LP, which is an existing gazetteer entity. Start and end are county-level only. Route not found, so no route is proposed. Intrastate, so FERC silence is expected; Texas Railroad Commission T-4 permit not checked. Tier high: three sources, but EIA and the trade items may trace to one company announcement. ProposalYear is the October 2010 announcement."
